1
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:06,569
Chapter 29 The recollection of about three days

2
00:00:06,569 --> 00:00:10,940
and nights succeeding this is very dim in my mind.

3
00:00:11,940 --> 00:00:16,980
I can recall some sensations felt in that interval, but few thoughts framed,

4
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:18,940
and no actions performed.

5
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:22,459
I knew I was in a small room and in a narrow bed.

6
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:24,739
To that bed, I seemed to have grown.

7
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:30,086
I lay on it motionless as a stone, and to have

8
00:00:30,088 --> 00:00:33,279
torn me from it would have been almost to kill me.

9
00:00:34,139 --> 00:00:39,019
I took no note of the lapse of time, of the change from morning to noon,

10
00:00:39,239 --> 00:00:40,279
from noon to evening.

11
00:00:41,839 --> 00:00:48,580
I observed, when anyone entered or left the apartment, I could even tell who they were.

12
00:00:48,940 --> 00:00:51,243
I could understand what was said when the

13
00:00:51,245 --> 00:00:55,021
speaker stood near to me, but I could not answer.

14
00:00:55,620 --> 00:00:59,139
To open my lips or move my limbs was equally impossible.

15
00:01:00,360 --> 00:01:04,099
Hanna, the servant, was my most frequent visitor.

16
00:01:04,959 --> 00:01:06,139
Her coming disturbed me.

17
00:01:06,720 --> 00:01:11,180
I had a feeling that she wished me away, that she did not understand me all my

18
00:01:11,180 --> 00:01:14,480
circumstances, that she was prejudiced against me.

19
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:21,180
Diana and Mary appeared in the chamber once or twice a day.

20
00:01:21,919 --> 00:01:24,940
They would whisper sentences of this sort at my bedside.

21
00:01:25,699 --> 00:01:28,279
It is very well we took her in.

22
00:01:29,480 --> 00:01:32,133
Yes, she would certainly have been found dead at the

23
00:01:32,135 --> 00:01:34,500
door in the morning had she been left out all night.

24
00:01:35,319 --> 00:01:37,040
I wonder what she has gone through.

25
00:01:38,540 --> 00:01:40,839
Strange hardships, I imagine.

26
00:01:41,839 --> 00:01:44,540
Poor, emaciated, pallid, wanderer.

27
00:01:45,459 --> 00:01:50,400
She is not an uneducated person, I should think, by her manner of speaking.

28
00:01:51,459 --> 00:01:53,080
Her accent was quite pure.

29
00:01:54,059 --> 00:01:59,760
And the clothes she took off, though splashed and wet, were little worn and fine.

30
00:02:00,459 --> 00:02:05,309
She has a peculiar face, fleshless and staggered as it is, I rather like it.

31
00:02:05,949 --> 00:02:11,771
And when in good health and animated, I can fancy her physiognomy would be agreeable.

32
00:02:12,430 --> 00:02:17,550
Never once in their dialogues did I hear a syllable of regret at the hospitality they

33
00:02:17,550 --> 00:02:22,190
had extended to me, or of suspicion of, or a version to myself.

34
00:02:23,129 --> 00:02:24,129
I was comforted.

35
00:02:25,650 --> 00:02:27,589
Mr. Singen came but once.

36
00:02:28,449 --> 00:02:32,410
He looked at me and said my state of lethargy was the

37
00:02:32,411 --> 00:02:36,290
result of reaction from excessive and protracted fatigue.

38
00:02:36,970 --> 00:02:40,410
He pronounced it needless to send for a doctor.

39
00:02:41,529 --> 00:02:45,349
Nature, he was sure, would manage best, left to herself.

40
00:02:46,410 --> 00:02:49,408
He said every nerve had been overstrained in some

41
00:02:49,408 --> 00:02:52,930
way, and the whole system must sleep torpid a while.

42
00:02:53,410 --> 00:02:54,410
There was no disease.

43
00:02:55,430 --> 00:02:59,510
He imagined my recovery would be rapid enough when once commenced.

44
00:03:00,010 --> 00:03:06,849
These opinions he delivered in a few words in a quiet, low voice, and added after a

45
00:03:06,851 --> 00:03:10,669
pause in the tone of a man little accustomed to expansive comment,

46
00:03:11,230 --> 00:03:17,391
rather an unusual physiognomy, certainly not indicative of vulgarity or degradation.

47
00:03:18,010 --> 00:03:20,370
Far otherwise responded Diana.

48
00:03:21,309 --> 00:03:25,849
To speak truth Singen, my heart rather warms to the poor little soul.

49
00:03:26,569 --> 00:03:29,690
I wish we may be able to benefit her permanently.

50
00:03:31,410 --> 00:03:34,470
That is hardly likely was the reply.

51
00:03:35,250 --> 00:03:40,010
You will find she is some young lady who has had a misunderstanding with her

52
00:03:40,010 --> 00:03:43,489
friends and has probably injudiciously left them.

53
00:03:44,089 --> 00:03:49,430
We may perhaps succeed in restoring her to them if she is not obstinate.

54
00:03:50,110 --> 00:03:56,250
But I trace lines of force in her face which make me skeptical of her tractability.

55
00:03:57,389 --> 00:04:01,711
He stood, considering me some minutes, then added,

56
00:04:01,713 --> 00:04:05,250
she looked sensible but not at all handsome.

57
00:04:06,129 --> 00:04:11,569
She is so ill Singen, ill or well she would always be plain, the grace and

58
00:04:11,571 --> 00:04:13,849
harmony of beauty are quite wanting in those features.

59
00:04:15,150 --> 00:04:16,870
On the third day I was better.

60
00:04:17,730 --> 00:04:22,870
On the fourth I could speak, move, rise in bed and turn.

61
00:04:24,010 --> 00:04:29,970
Hannah had brought me some gruel and dry toast about, as I supposed, the dinner hour.

62
00:04:30,050 --> 00:04:35,190
I had eaten with relish, the food was good, void of the feverish flavor which

63
00:04:35,190 --> 00:04:37,230
had hitherto poisoned what I had swallowed.

64
00:04:37,690 --> 00:04:41,750
When she left me I felt comparatively strong and revived.

65
00:04:42,769 --> 00:04:46,610
Air-long satiety of repose and desire for action stirred me.

66
00:04:47,309 --> 00:04:49,989
I wished to rise, but what could I put on?

67
00:04:50,389 --> 00:04:53,692
Only my damp and bemyered apparel, in which I

68
00:04:53,692 --> 00:04:56,491
had slept on the ground and fallen in the marsh.

69
00:04:57,709 --> 00:05:04,150
I felt ashamed to appear before my benefactors so clad, I was spared the humiliation.

70
00:05:05,410 --> 00:05:09,430
On a chair by the bedside were all my own things, clean and dry.

71
00:05:10,589 --> 00:05:13,110
My black silk frock hung against the wall.

72
00:05:14,169 --> 00:05:16,629
The traces of the bog were removed from it.

73
00:05:17,349 --> 00:05:21,209
The creases left by the wet smoothed out it was quite decent.

74
00:05:22,250 --> 00:05:26,529
My very shoes and stockings were purified and rendered presentable.

75
00:05:27,230 --> 00:05:33,271
There were the means of washing in the room and a comb and brush to smooth my hair.

76
00:05:34,089 --> 00:05:41,131
After a weary process and resting every five minutes, I succeeded in dressing myself.

77
00:05:41,750 --> 00:05:47,330
My clothes hung loose on me, for I was much wasted, but I covered deficiencies

78
00:05:47,330 --> 00:05:53,110
with a shawl and once more clean and respectable looking, no speck of the dirt,

79
00:05:53,769 --> 00:05:59,709
no trace of the disorder I so hated, and which seemed so to degrade me left.

80
00:06:00,989 --> 00:06:06,569
I crept down a stone staircase with the aid of the bannisters, to a narrow low

81
00:06:06,571 --> 00:06:10,069
passage and found my way presently to the kitchen.

82
00:06:11,290 --> 00:06:16,610
It was full of the fragrance of new bread and the warmth of a generous fire.

83
00:06:16,610 --> 00:06:18,769
Hannah was baking.

84
00:06:19,790 --> 00:06:24,809
Prejudices, it is well known, are most difficult to eradicate from the heart,

85
00:06:25,410 --> 00:06:29,069
whose soil has never been loosened or fertilized by education.

86
00:06:29,709 --> 00:06:33,510
They grow there, firm as weeds among stones.

87
00:06:34,790 --> 00:06:37,730
Hannah had been cold and stiff indeed at the first.

88
00:06:38,629 --> 00:06:41,898
Laterally, she had begun to lent a little, and when she

89
00:06:41,900 --> 00:06:45,220
saw me come in tidy and well dressed, she even smiled.

90
00:06:46,739 --> 00:06:47,220
What?

91
00:06:47,760 --> 00:06:49,400
You have got up, she said.

92
00:06:50,220 --> 00:06:51,220
You are better than.

93
00:06:51,980 --> 00:06:55,540
You may sit you down in my chair on the hearth stone, if you will.

94
00:06:56,839 --> 00:06:59,620
She pointed to the rocking chair, I took it.

95
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:05,760
She bustled about, examining me every now and then with the corner of her eye,

96
00:07:06,480 --> 00:07:10,819
turning to me, as she took some loaves from the oven, she asked bluntly.

97
00:07:11,860 --> 00:07:14,040
Did you ever go a begging or four you came here?

98
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:20,779
I was indignant for a moment, but remembering that anger was out of the

99
00:07:20,781 --> 00:07:26,639
question, and that I had indeed appeared as a beggar to her, I answered quietly.

100
00:07:27,559 --> 00:07:30,720
But still not without a certain marked firmness.

101
00:07:31,519 --> 00:07:34,160
You are mistaken in supposing me a beggar.

102
00:07:34,660 --> 00:07:35,660
I am no beggar.

103
00:07:36,059 --> 00:07:38,480
Any more than yourself or your young ladies.

104
00:07:39,519 --> 00:07:43,440
After a pause, she said, I don't understand that.

105
00:07:44,239 --> 00:07:46,400
You have like no house nor no brass, I guess?

106
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:51,760
The want of house or brass by which I suppose you mean

107
00:07:51,760 --> 00:07:54,800
money does not make a beggar in your sense of the word.

108
00:07:56,639 --> 00:07:58,639
Are you book learned?

109
00:07:59,260 --> 00:08:00,639
She inquired presently.

110
00:08:01,080 --> 00:08:02,080
Yes, very.

111
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:04,919
But you've never been to a boarding school.

112
00:08:06,160 --> 00:08:08,419
I was at a boarding school eight years.

113
00:08:09,620 --> 00:08:10,900
She opened her eyes wide.

114
00:08:12,239 --> 00:08:14,720
Whatever, cannot you keep yourself for then.

115
00:08:16,059 --> 00:08:20,019
I have kept myself, and I trust she'll keep myself again.

116
00:08:21,260 --> 00:08:23,199
What are you going to do with these gooseberries?

117
00:08:23,839 --> 00:08:26,919
I inquired, as she brought out a basket of the fruit.

118
00:08:28,239 --> 00:08:29,239
Mac I'm into pies?

119
00:08:30,239 --> 00:08:31,900
Give them to me, and I'll pick them.

120
00:08:33,099 --> 00:08:35,500
Nay, I don't want you to do not.

121
00:08:36,580 --> 00:08:38,059
But I must do something.

122
00:08:38,580 --> 00:08:39,580
Let me have them.

123
00:08:40,019 --> 00:08:44,519
She consented, and she even brought me a clean towel to spread over my dress.

124
00:08:45,699 --> 00:08:48,459
Lest, as she said, I should mucky it.

125
00:08:49,959 --> 00:08:51,959
You've not been used to Sarvant's walk.

126
00:08:52,419 --> 00:08:54,620
I see by your hands, she remarked.

127
00:08:55,980 --> 00:08:57,540
Happen you've been a dressmaker.

128
00:08:58,580 --> 00:08:59,860
No, you are wrong.

129
00:09:00,819 --> 00:09:03,319
And now, never mind what I have been.

130
00:09:04,379 --> 00:09:06,247
Don't trouble your head further about me, but

131
00:09:06,247 --> 00:09:09,440
tell me the name of the house where we are.

132
00:09:10,180 --> 00:09:14,160
Some cause it marsh end, and some cause it moor house.

133
00:09:15,040 --> 00:09:18,519
And the gentleman who lives here is called Mr. Sinjin.

134
00:09:19,739 --> 00:09:24,540
Nay, he doesn't live here, he's only staying a while, when he is at home,

135
00:09:24,699 --> 00:09:26,519
he is in his own parish at Morton.

136
00:09:27,419 --> 00:09:29,519
That village a few miles off, I.

137
00:09:30,300 --> 00:09:31,319
And what is he?

138
00:09:32,160 --> 00:09:33,160
He is a person.

139
00:09:34,540 --> 00:09:37,769
I remembered the answer of the old housekeeper at

140
00:09:37,771 --> 00:09:40,580
the Parsonage, when I had asked to see the clergyman.

141
00:09:41,639 --> 00:09:43,839
This then was his father's residence.

142
00:09:45,220 --> 00:09:50,180
I, old Mr. Rivers lived here, and his father and grandfather and Gert,

143
00:09:50,860 --> 00:09:52,919
great grandfather, are for him.

144
00:09:54,099 --> 00:09:57,779
The name then of that gentleman is Mr. Sinjin Rivers.

145
00:09:59,739 --> 00:10:02,379
I, Sinjin is like his cursed name.

146
00:10:03,440 --> 00:10:05,580
And his sisters are called Diana and Mary Rivers?

147
00:10:06,500 --> 00:10:07,500
Yes.

148
00:10:07,860 --> 00:10:08,860
Their father is dead?

149
00:10:09,900 --> 00:10:11,480
Dead three weeks, sin of a stroke.

150
00:10:12,800 --> 00:10:13,800
They have no mother.

151
00:10:15,260 --> 00:10:17,980
The mistress has been dead this money a year.

152
00:10:19,099 --> 00:10:20,699
Have you lived with the family long?

153
00:10:21,860 --> 00:10:24,360
I've lived here 30 years, I nursed them all three.

154
00:10:25,599 --> 00:10:28,339
That proves you must have been an honest and faithful servant.

155
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:34,461
I will say so much for you, though you have had the inability to call me a beggar.

156
00:10:35,120 --> 00:10:39,180
She again regarded me with a surprised stare.

157
00:10:40,559 --> 00:10:45,080
I believe, she said, I was quite mistaken in my thoughts of you.

158
00:10:45,919 --> 00:10:48,699
But there is so many cheats goes about human foggy me.

159
00:10:50,180 --> 00:10:58,059
And though, I continued, rather severely, you wished to turn me from the door on a

160
00:10:58,061 --> 00:11:00,739
night when you should not have shut out a dog.

161
00:11:01,559 --> 00:11:04,839
Well, it was hard, but what can a body do?

162
00:11:06,059 --> 00:11:09,160
I thought more of the children or of myself poor things.

163
00:11:09,959 --> 00:11:11,919
They've liked nobody to take care on and but me.

164
00:11:12,339 --> 00:11:13,580
I'm like to look sharpish.

165
00:11:14,500 --> 00:11:17,319
I maintained a grave silence for some minutes.

166
00:11:18,580 --> 00:11:20,639
You wouldn't think too hardly of me.

167
00:11:21,339 --> 00:11:22,599
She again remarked.

168
00:11:23,680 --> 00:11:26,540
But I do think hardly of you, I said.

169
00:11:27,239 --> 00:11:28,639
And I'll tell you why.

170
00:11:29,720 --> 00:11:34,720
Not so much because you refused to give me shelter or regarded me as an imposter,

171
00:11:35,819 --> 00:11:38,720
as because you just now made it a species of

172
00:11:38,720 --> 00:11:42,421
reproach that I had no brass and no house.

173
00:11:42,800 --> 00:11:47,559
Some of the best people that ever lived have been as destitute as I am.

174
00:11:48,400 --> 00:11:52,120
And if you are a Christian, you ought not to consider poverty or crime.

175
00:11:53,739 --> 00:11:55,860
No more I ought," said she.

176
00:11:56,680 --> 00:11:58,339
Mr. Syngin tells me so too.

177
00:11:59,300 --> 00:12:03,720
And I see I were rang, but I've clear a different notion on you now to what I had.

178
00:12:04,599 --> 00:12:07,540
You look a rate down decent little crater.

179
00:12:08,400 --> 00:12:09,459
That will do.

180
00:12:09,860 --> 00:12:10,860
I forgive you now.

181
00:12:11,339 --> 00:12:12,339
Shake hands.

182
00:12:12,860 --> 00:12:15,959
She put her flowery and horny hand into mine.

183
00:12:16,919 --> 00:12:20,120
Another in hearty a smile illumined her rough face.

184
00:12:20,900 --> 00:12:23,139
And from that moment we were friends.

185
00:12:25,480 --> 00:12:28,000
Hannah was evidently fond of talking.

186
00:12:29,059 --> 00:12:33,819
While I picked the fruit and she made the paste for the ice, she proceeded to give

187
00:12:33,821 --> 00:12:38,599
me sundry details about her deceased master and mistress and the children,

188
00:12:39,239 --> 00:12:40,559
as she called the young people.

189
00:12:41,819 --> 00:12:46,548
Old Mr. Rivers, she said, was a plain man enough, but a

190
00:12:46,548 --> 00:12:50,519
gentleman, and of as ancient a family as could be found.

191
00:12:51,800 --> 00:12:55,519
Marshend had belonged to the rivers ever since it was a house.

192
00:12:56,379 --> 00:13:02,660
And it was, she affirmed, a boon two hundred year old, for all it looked but a

193
00:13:02,661 --> 00:13:09,561
small humble place, not to compare with Mr. Oliver's grand hall down in Morton Vale.

194
00:13:09,940 --> 00:13:14,760
But she could remember Bill Oliver's father, a journeyman needlemaker.

195
00:13:15,779 --> 00:13:21,480
And the rivers were gentry, the old days of the Henry's, as anybody might see by

196
00:13:21,480 --> 00:13:24,059
looking into the registers in Morton Church Vestry.

197
00:13:25,260 --> 00:13:26,639
Still, she allowed.

198
00:13:27,980 --> 00:13:31,459
The old maester was like other folk, not mish out at a

199
00:13:31,461 --> 00:13:35,000
common way, start mad at shooting and farming and sitch-like.

200
00:13:37,180 --> 00:13:38,839
The mistress was different.

201
00:13:39,639 --> 00:13:44,919
She was a great reader and studied a deal, and the bans had taken after her.

202
00:13:45,879 --> 00:13:49,220
There was nothing like them in these pots, nor ever had been.

203
00:13:49,720 --> 00:13:54,440
They had liked learning, all three, almost from the time they could speak.

204
00:13:55,540 --> 00:13:59,419
And they had always been, of a mack of their own.

205
00:14:00,459 --> 00:14:04,660
Mr. Sinjin, when he grew up, would go to college and be a person.

206
00:14:05,279 --> 00:14:10,459
And the girls, as soon as they left school, would seek places as governorses,

207
00:14:10,959 --> 00:14:15,620
for they had told her their father had some years ago lost a great deal of money.

208
00:14:16,160 --> 00:14:22,480
By a man he had trusted, turning bankrupt, and as he was now not rich enough to give

209
00:14:22,480 --> 00:14:26,120
them fortunes, they must provide for themselves.

210
00:14:27,260 --> 00:14:33,199
They had lived very little at home for a long while, and were only come now to stay

211
00:14:33,201 --> 00:14:35,660
a few weeks on account of their father's death.

212
00:14:36,459 --> 00:14:42,599
But they did so like Marsh End and Morton, and all these moors and hills about.

213
00:14:43,660 --> 00:14:49,459
They had been in London, and many other grand towns, but they always said there

214
00:14:49,461 --> 00:14:52,864
was no place like home, and then they were so

215
00:14:52,866 --> 00:14:57,500
agreeable with each other, never fell out nor threaped.

216
00:14:58,599 --> 00:15:01,919
She did not know where there was such a family for being united.

217
00:15:03,339 --> 00:15:06,580
Having finished my task of Gooseberry picking, I

218
00:15:06,580 --> 00:15:09,381
asked where the two ladies and their brother were now.

219
00:15:10,720 --> 00:15:16,080
Gone over to Morton for a walk, but they would be back in half an hour to tea.

220
00:15:16,580 --> 00:15:19,800
They returned within the time Hannah had allotted them.

221
00:15:20,540 --> 00:15:22,180
They entered by the kitchen door.

222
00:15:23,500 --> 00:15:27,559
Mr. Sinjian, when he saw me, merely bowed and passed through.

223
00:15:28,500 --> 00:15:29,660
The two ladies stopped.

224
00:15:30,519 --> 00:15:35,703
Mary, in a few words, kindly and calmly expressed the pleasure

225
00:15:35,705 --> 00:15:38,839
she felt in seeing me well enough to be able to come down.

226
00:15:40,099 --> 00:15:41,400
Diana took my hand.

227
00:15:41,980 --> 00:15:43,019
She shook her head at me.

228
00:15:44,239 --> 00:15:46,860
You should have waited for my leave to descend, she said.

229
00:15:47,760 --> 00:15:52,620
You still look very pale and so thin, poor child, poor girl.

230
00:15:53,919 --> 00:15:58,220
Diana had a voice toned to my ear, like the cooling of a dove.

231
00:15:59,519 --> 00:16:03,220
She possessed eyes whose gaze I delighted to encounter.

232
00:16:04,139 --> 00:16:06,139
Her whole face seemed to me full of charm.

233
00:16:07,500 --> 00:16:09,919
Mary's countenance was equally intelligent.

234
00:16:10,559 --> 00:16:14,925
Her features equally pretty, but her expression was more

235
00:16:14,927 --> 00:16:18,500
reserved, and her manners, though, gentle, more distant.

236
00:16:20,019 --> 00:16:22,860
Diana looked and spoke with a certain authority.

237
00:16:23,639 --> 00:16:25,980
She had a will evidently.

238
00:16:26,639 --> 00:16:31,339
It was my nature to feel pleasure in yielding to an authority supported like

239
00:16:31,341 --> 00:16:37,500
hers, and to bend where my conscience and self-respect permitted to an active will.

240
00:16:39,400 --> 00:16:42,500
And what business have you here, she continued.

241
00:16:43,540 --> 00:16:44,839
It is not your place.

242
00:16:45,760 --> 00:16:49,099
Mary and I sit in the kitchen sometimes because at home we like to be free,

243
00:16:49,300 --> 00:16:53,860
even to license, but you are a visitor and must go into the parlour.

244
00:16:54,839 --> 00:16:57,747
I am very well here, not at all, with Hannah

245
00:16:57,747 --> 00:17:00,540
bustling about and covering you with flour.

246
00:17:01,360 --> 00:17:05,199
Besides, the fire is too hot for you, interposed Mary.

247
00:17:05,900 --> 00:17:10,639
To be sure, added her sister, come, you must be obedient.

248
00:17:11,639 --> 00:17:16,839
And still holding my hand, she made me rise, and led me into the inner room.

249
00:17:18,180 --> 00:17:21,955
Sit there, she said, placing me on the sofa, while

250
00:17:21,957 --> 00:17:25,201
we take our things off and get the tea ready.

251
00:17:25,480 --> 00:17:31,080
It is another privilege we exercise in our little moorland home, to prepare our own

252
00:17:31,080 --> 00:17:35,360
meals when we are so inclined, or when Hannah is baking, brewing,

253
00:17:35,660 --> 00:17:36,839
washing, or ironing.

254
00:17:37,940 --> 00:17:43,156
She closed the door, leaving me solace with Mr. Sinjin,

255
00:17:43,158 --> 00:17:46,699
who sat opposite a book or newspaper in his hand.

256
00:17:47,800 --> 00:17:52,580
I examined first the parlour, and then it's occupant.

257
00:17:53,160 --> 00:17:57,860
The parlour was rather a small room, very plainly furnished, yet comfortable,

258
00:17:58,400 --> 00:17:59,400
because clean and neat.

259
00:18:00,580 --> 00:18:03,625
The old-fashioned chairs were very bright, and

260
00:18:03,627 --> 00:18:06,781
the walnut wood table was like a looking glass.

261
00:18:10,080 --> 00:18:18,080
A few strange antique portraits of the glass doors contained some books,

262
00:18:18,779 --> 00:18:20,279
and an ancient set of china.

263
00:18:20,760 --> 00:18:23,199
There was no superfluous ornament in the room.

264
00:18:23,940 --> 00:18:28,540
Not one modern piece of furniture, save a brace of workboxes, and a ladies

265
00:18:28,540 --> 00:18:34,540
desk in Rosewood, which stood on a side table, everything, including the carpet

266
00:18:34,540 --> 00:18:38,760
and curtains, looked at once well-worn and well-saved.

267
00:18:40,139 --> 00:18:47,019
Mr. Sinjin, sitting as still as one of the dusty pictures on the walls, keeping his

268
00:18:47,021 --> 00:18:50,737
eyes fixed on the page he perused, and his

269
00:18:50,737 --> 00:18:54,059
lips mutely sealed, was easy enough to examine.

270
00:18:55,419 --> 00:18:59,720
Had he been a statue instead of a man, he could not have been easier.

271
00:19:00,620 --> 00:19:04,940
He was young, perhaps from 28 to 30, tall, slender.

272
00:19:05,760 --> 00:19:07,440
His face riveted the eye.

273
00:19:08,040 --> 00:19:13,839
It was like a Greek face, very pure in outline, quite a straight, classic nose,

274
00:19:14,760 --> 00:19:16,540
quite an Athenian mouth and chin.

275
00:19:17,660 --> 00:19:23,739
It is seldom indeed, an English face comes so near the antique models as did his.

276
00:19:24,959 --> 00:19:28,440
He might well be a little shocked at the irregularity of my lineaments,

277
00:19:29,279 --> 00:19:31,599
his own being so harmonious.

278
00:19:32,720 --> 00:19:38,680
His eyes were large and blue, with brown lashes, his high forehead, colourless as

279
00:19:38,680 --> 00:19:42,919
ivory, was partially streaked over by careless locks of fair hair.

280
00:19:44,379 --> 00:19:47,199
This is a gentle delineation, is it not reader?

281
00:19:48,459 --> 00:19:53,319
Yet he, whom it describes, scarcely impressed one with the idea of a gentle,

282
00:19:53,699 --> 00:19:57,879
a yielding, an impressible, or even of a placid nature.

283
00:19:58,839 --> 00:20:04,639
Cuesant as he now sat, there was something about his nostril, his mouth, his brow,

284
00:20:05,419 --> 00:20:11,940
which to my perceptions, indicated elements within either restless or hard or eager.

285
00:20:12,120 --> 00:20:17,379
He did not speak to me one word, nor even direct to me one glance,

286
00:20:18,180 --> 00:20:19,300
till his sisters returned.

287
00:20:20,319 --> 00:20:25,739
Diana, as she passed in and out, in the course of preparing tea,

288
00:20:26,400 --> 00:20:29,120
brought me a little cake, baked on the top of the oven.

289
00:20:30,019 --> 00:20:32,819
Eat that now, she said, you must be hungry.

290
00:20:33,919 --> 00:20:37,160
Hannah says you have had nothing but some gruel since breakfast.

291
00:20:38,760 --> 00:20:40,160
I did not refuse it.

292
00:20:40,739 --> 00:20:42,879
For my appetite was awakened and keen.

293
00:20:43,919 --> 00:20:48,879
Mr. Rivers now closed his book, approached the table, and as he took a

294
00:20:48,881 --> 00:20:53,580
seat, fixed his blue, pictorial-looking eyes, full on me.

295
00:20:54,540 --> 00:20:59,940
There was an unceremonious directness, a searching-decided steadfastness in his

296
00:20:59,940 --> 00:21:04,122
gaze now, which told that intention and not-diffidence

297
00:21:04,122 --> 00:21:06,800
had hitherto kept it averted from the stranger.

298
00:21:07,800 --> 00:21:10,300
You are very hungry, he said.

299
00:21:11,199 --> 00:21:12,199
I am, sir.

300
00:21:12,980 --> 00:21:13,980
It is my way.

301
00:21:14,559 --> 00:21:19,480
It always was my way, by instinct, ever to meet the brief with brevity,

302
00:21:20,180 --> 00:21:21,580
the direct with plainness.

303
00:21:22,800 --> 00:21:24,591
It is well for you that a low fever has

304
00:21:24,593 --> 00:21:28,080
forced you to abstain for the last three days.

305
00:21:28,300 --> 00:21:32,419
There would have been danger in yielding to the cravings of your appetite at first.

306
00:21:33,540 --> 00:21:36,959
Now you may eat, though still not immoderately.

307
00:21:38,940 --> 00:21:42,580
I trust I shall not eat long at your expense, sir,

308
00:21:42,580 --> 00:21:45,739
was my very clumsily contrived, unpolished answer.

309
00:21:47,339 --> 00:21:49,160
No, he said coolly.

310
00:21:49,819 --> 00:21:53,254
When you have indicated to us the residence of your friends,

311
00:21:53,256 --> 00:21:56,959
we can write to them, and you may be restored to home.

312
00:21:58,160 --> 00:22:01,686
That, I must plainly tell you, is out of my power

313
00:22:01,688 --> 00:22:04,800
to do, being absolutely without home and friends.

314
00:22:05,900 --> 00:22:09,239
The three looked at me, but not distrustfully.

315
00:22:10,160 --> 00:22:12,720
I felt there was no suspicion in their glances.

316
00:22:13,540 --> 00:22:14,860
There was more of curiosity.

317
00:22:15,739 --> 00:22:22,500
I speak particularly of the young ladies, Syngen's eyes, though clear enough in a

318
00:22:22,500 --> 00:22:26,599
literal sense in a figurative one, were difficult to fathom.

319
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:31,641
He seemed to use them rather as instruments to search

320
00:22:31,642 --> 00:22:35,900
other people's thoughts than as agents to reveal his own.

321
00:22:36,699 --> 00:22:39,779
The which combination of keenness and reserve was

322
00:22:39,779 --> 00:22:43,900
considerably more calculated to embarrass than to encourage.

323
00:22:45,620 --> 00:22:51,360
Do you mean to say, he asked, that you are completely isolated from every connection?

324
00:22:52,500 --> 00:22:53,500
I do.

325
00:22:54,080 --> 00:22:56,139
Not a tie links me to any living thing.

326
00:22:57,139 --> 00:23:00,279
Not a claim do I possess to admittance under any roof in England?

327
00:23:01,599 --> 00:23:04,760
The most singular position at your age.

328
00:23:05,760 --> 00:23:10,339
Here I saw his glance directed to my hands, which were folded on the table before me.

329
00:23:10,341 --> 00:23:12,779
I wondered what he sought there.

330
00:23:13,839 --> 00:23:16,059
His words soon explained the quest.

331
00:23:17,099 --> 00:23:18,220
You have never been married?

332
00:23:19,160 --> 00:23:20,160
You're a spinster?

333
00:23:20,739 --> 00:23:21,739
Diana laughed.

334
00:23:22,019 --> 00:23:28,300
Why, she can't be above 17 or 18 years old, Syngen, said she, I am near 19,

335
00:23:28,760 --> 00:23:29,760
but I am not married.

336
00:23:30,160 --> 00:23:31,160
No.

337
00:23:31,199 --> 00:23:34,419
I felt a burning glow mount to my face.

338
00:23:35,139 --> 00:23:39,599
For bitter and agitating recollections were awakened by the illusion to marriage.

339
00:23:40,339 --> 00:23:43,519
They all saw the embarrassment and the emotion.

340
00:23:44,919 --> 00:23:51,141
Diana and Mary relieved me by turning their eyes elsewhere than to my crimsoned visage.

341
00:23:51,660 --> 00:23:55,199
But the colder and sterner brother continued to gaze, till

342
00:23:55,199 --> 00:23:59,819
the trouble he had excited forced out tears as well as color.

343
00:24:01,000 --> 00:24:02,860
Where did you last reside?

344
00:24:03,519 --> 00:24:04,519
He now asked.

345
00:24:05,059 --> 00:24:09,440
You are too inquisitive, Syngen, murmured Mary in a low voice.

346
00:24:10,300 --> 00:24:12,150
But he leaned over the table and required an

347
00:24:12,152 --> 00:24:15,220
answer by a second firm and piercing look.

348
00:24:16,860 --> 00:24:20,805
The name of the place where and of the person with

349
00:24:20,807 --> 00:24:24,120
whom I lived is my secret I replied concisely.

350
00:24:25,599 --> 00:24:31,739
Which, if you like, you have, in my opinion, a right to keep both from Syngen

351
00:24:31,741 --> 00:24:34,300
and every other questioner, remarked Diana.

352
00:24:35,279 --> 00:24:39,819
Yet, if I know nothing about you or your history, I cannot help you, he said.

353
00:24:40,699 --> 00:24:41,699
And you need help?

354
00:24:42,080 --> 00:24:43,080
Do you not?

355
00:24:43,860 --> 00:24:44,860
I need it.

356
00:24:45,160 --> 00:24:49,491
And I seek it so far, sir, that some true philanthropist

357
00:24:49,493 --> 00:24:52,519
will put me in the way of getting work which I can do.

358
00:24:53,339 --> 00:24:56,209
And the remuneration for which will keep me,

359
00:24:56,209 --> 00:24:59,940
if but in the barest necessaries of life.

360
00:25:00,860 --> 00:25:05,279
I know not whether I am a true philanthropist, yet I am willing to aid

361
00:25:05,281 --> 00:25:08,559
you to the utmost of my power in a purpose so honest.

362
00:25:09,879 --> 00:25:15,360
First then, tell me what you have been accustomed to do and what you can do.

363
00:25:16,540 --> 00:25:18,919
I had now swallowed my tea.

364
00:25:20,180 --> 00:25:25,379
I was mightily refreshed by the beverage, as much so as a giant with wine.

365
00:25:26,360 --> 00:25:29,608
It gave new tone to my unstrung nerves and enabled

366
00:25:29,610 --> 00:25:32,839
me to address this penetrating young judge steadily.

367
00:25:34,319 --> 00:25:38,375
Mr. Rivers, I said, turning to him and looking at

368
00:25:38,377 --> 00:25:41,819
him as he looked at me openly and without dividends.

369
00:25:43,180 --> 00:25:47,040
You and your sisters have done me a great service.

370
00:25:47,550 --> 00:25:50,540
The greatest man can do his fellow being.

371
00:25:51,239 --> 00:25:55,699
You have rescued me by your noble hospitality from death.

372
00:25:56,239 --> 00:26:02,980
This benefit conferred gives you an unlimited claim on my gratitude and a

373
00:26:02,980 --> 00:26:06,040
claim to a certain extent on my confidence.

374
00:26:07,360 --> 00:26:11,500
I will tell you as much of the history of the wanderer you have harbored,

375
00:26:12,019 --> 00:26:17,900
as I can tell without compromising my own peace of mind, my own security,

376
00:26:18,580 --> 00:26:21,500
moral and physical, and that of others.

377
00:26:22,500 --> 00:26:25,607
I am an orphan, the daughter of a clergyman,

378
00:26:25,608 --> 00:26:28,881
my parents died before I could know them.

379
00:26:28,919 --> 00:26:33,360
I was brought up a dependent, educated in a charitable institution.

380
00:26:34,720 --> 00:26:37,932
I will even tell you the name of the establishment,

381
00:26:37,932 --> 00:26:41,980
where I passed six years as a pupil and two as a teacher.

382
00:26:43,160 --> 00:26:44,639
Lowwood orphan asylum.

383
00:26:45,419 --> 00:26:46,419
Shire.

384
00:26:46,599 --> 00:26:48,559
You will have heard of it, Mr. Rivers.

385
00:26:49,919 --> 00:26:52,400
The Reverend Robert Brocklehurst is the treasurer.

386
00:26:53,580 --> 00:26:56,980
I have heard of Mr. Brocklehurst and I have seen the school.

387
00:26:58,319 --> 00:27:02,639
I left Lowwood nearly a year since to become a private governor.

388
00:27:03,239 --> 00:27:06,220
I obtained a good situation and was happy.

389
00:27:07,059 --> 00:27:11,839
This place I was obliged to leave four days before I came here.

390
00:27:12,900 --> 00:27:16,639
The reason of my departure I cannot and ought not to explain.

391
00:27:17,480 --> 00:27:21,279
It would be useless, dangerous, and would sound incredible.

392
00:27:22,139 --> 00:27:23,519
No blame attached to me.

393
00:27:24,480 --> 00:27:27,599
I am as free from culpability as any one of you three.

394
00:27:29,040 --> 00:27:32,419
Miserable I am, and must be for a time.

395
00:27:33,220 --> 00:27:35,788
For the catastrophe which drove me from a house I had

396
00:27:35,788 --> 00:27:38,940
found a paradise was of a strange and dire full nature.

397
00:27:39,919 --> 00:27:43,059
I observed but two points in planning my departure.

398
00:27:43,879 --> 00:27:49,680
Speed, secrecy, to secure these I had to leave behind me everything I possessed

399
00:27:49,680 --> 00:27:54,472
except a small parcel, which in my hurry and trouble of mind I

400
00:27:54,474 --> 00:27:57,620
forgot to take out of the coach that brought me to Whitcross.

401
00:27:58,540 --> 00:28:03,019
To this neighborhood then I came quite destitute.

402
00:28:03,680 --> 00:28:06,536
I slept two nights in the open air and wandered

403
00:28:06,538 --> 00:28:09,760
about two days without crossing a threshold.

404
00:28:10,160 --> 00:28:13,720
But twice in that space of time did I taste food.

405
00:28:14,839 --> 00:28:21,000
And it was when brought by hunger, exhaustion, and despair almost to the last

406
00:28:21,000 --> 00:28:26,216
gasp that you, Mr. Rivers, forbade me to perish of want

407
00:28:26,216 --> 00:28:30,059
at your door and took me under the shelter of your roof.

408
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:33,963
I know all your sisters have done for me since, for

409
00:28:33,963 --> 00:28:36,980
I have not been insensible during my seeming torpor.

410
00:28:37,919 --> 00:28:41,749
And I owe to their spontaneous, genuine, genial

411
00:28:41,750 --> 00:28:46,120
compassion as larger debt as to your evangelical charity.

412
00:28:48,019 --> 00:28:53,000
Don't make her talk anymore now, Sinjin, said Diana, as I paused.

413
00:28:53,760 --> 00:28:56,239
She is evidently not yet fit for excitement.

414
00:28:57,180 --> 00:28:58,980
Come to the sofa and sit down now Miss Elliot.

415
00:29:00,360 --> 00:29:07,281
I gave an involuntary half-start at hearing the alias I had forgotten my new name.

416
00:29:07,779 --> 00:29:12,260
Mr. Rivers, whom nothing seemed to escape, noticed it at once.

417
00:29:13,459 --> 00:29:14,940
You said your name was Jane Elliot.

418
00:29:15,620 --> 00:29:16,620
He observed.

419
00:29:17,239 --> 00:29:18,239
I did say so.

420
00:29:18,739 --> 00:29:22,260
And it is the name by which I think it expedient to be called at present.

421
00:29:23,059 --> 00:29:27,180
But it is not my real name, and when I hear it, it sounds strange to me.

422
00:29:28,639 --> 00:29:30,180
Your real name you will not give.

423
00:29:31,699 --> 00:29:32,699
No.

424
00:29:32,959 --> 00:29:38,940
I fear discovery above all things, and whatever disclosure would lead to it, I avoid.

425
00:29:39,660 --> 00:29:42,099
You are quite right, I am sure, said Diana.

426
00:29:42,720 --> 00:29:45,660
Now do brother, let her be at peace a while.

427
00:29:46,940 --> 00:29:50,508
But when Sinjin had mused a few moments, he recommenced

428
00:29:50,508 --> 00:29:53,839
as imperturbably and with as much acumen as ever.

429
00:29:55,720 --> 00:29:59,220
You would not like to be long dependent on our hospitality.

430
00:30:00,120 --> 00:30:05,680
You would wish, I see, to dispense as soon as maybe with my sister's compassion.

431
00:30:06,519 --> 00:30:10,133
And above all, with my charity, I am quite sensible of

432
00:30:10,135 --> 00:30:13,440
the distinction drawn, nor do I resent it, it is just.

433
00:30:15,019 --> 00:30:17,059
You desire to be independent of us?

434
00:30:17,779 --> 00:30:18,779
I do.

435
00:30:19,019 --> 00:30:20,260
I have already said so.

436
00:30:20,779 --> 00:30:24,620
Show me how to work, or how to seek work, that is all I now ask.

437
00:30:24,839 --> 00:30:27,800
Then let me go, if it be but to the meanest cottage.

438
00:30:27,800 --> 00:30:31,415
But till then, allow me to stay here, I dread

439
00:30:31,415 --> 00:30:35,379
another essay of the horrors of homeless destitution.

440
00:30:36,699 --> 00:30:42,139
Indeed you shall stay here, said Diana, putting her white hand on my head.

441
00:30:43,139 --> 00:30:46,724
You shall, repeated Mary, in the tone of

442
00:30:46,724 --> 00:30:50,860
undemonstrative sincerity which seemed natural to her.

443
00:30:51,839 --> 00:30:58,099
My sisters, you see, have a pleasure in keeping you, said Mr. Shingen.

444
00:30:58,680 --> 00:31:03,040
As they would have a pleasure in keeping and cherishing a half-frozen bird,

445
00:31:03,860 --> 00:31:06,660
some wintry wind might have driven through their casement.

446
00:31:07,459 --> 00:31:11,072
I feel more inclination to put you in the way of

447
00:31:11,072 --> 00:31:14,139
keeping yourself, and shall endeavour to do so.

448
00:31:14,760 --> 00:31:17,919
But observe, my sphere is narrow.

449
00:31:18,980 --> 00:31:21,699
I am but the incumbent of a poor country -parish.

450
00:31:22,360 --> 00:31:24,440
My aid must be of the humblest sort.

451
00:31:25,699 --> 00:31:29,595
And if you are inclined to despise the day of small things,

452
00:31:29,595 --> 00:31:32,900
seek some more efficient sucker than such as I can offer.

453
00:31:34,819 --> 00:31:39,519
She has already said that she is willing to do anything honest she can do.

454
00:31:40,519 --> 00:31:41,839
Answered Diana for me.

455
00:31:43,080 --> 00:31:44,080
And you know Shingen?

456
00:31:44,819 --> 00:31:46,879
She has no choice of helpers.

457
00:31:47,459 --> 00:31:50,879
She is forced to put up with such crusty people as you.

458
00:31:52,440 --> 00:31:53,599
I will be a dressmaker.

459
00:31:54,419 --> 00:31:56,139
I will be a plain workwoman.

460
00:31:56,959 --> 00:31:59,680
I will be a servant, a nursegirl.

461
00:32:00,160 --> 00:32:02,559
If I can be no better, I answered.

462
00:32:03,339 --> 00:32:06,480
Right, said Mr. Shingen, quite cooly.

463
00:32:07,379 --> 00:32:12,300
If such is your spirit, I promised to aid you in my own time and way.

464
00:32:13,599 --> 00:32:17,559
He now resumed the book with which he had been occupied before tea.

465
00:32:18,919 --> 00:32:23,249
I soon withdrew, for I had talked as much and sat

466
00:32:23,250 --> 00:32:27,080
up as long as my present strength would permit.
